# Engineering Guardrails

Follow `CLAUDE.md` for the full ruleset. Non-negotiables:

- Strict typing: pydantic models or TypedDict at every API boundary. No `Any`, no untyped `dict`.
- No empty `except`/`catch`. Network calls require timeout + exponential-backoff retry.
- Secrets only via env vars — never hardcode keys, tokens, or staging URLs.
- No blocking calls on the main/UI thread; no redundant network polling.
- Mobile: batch network calls, exponential backoff when offline, offline-first local cache, no memory leaks (listeners/subscriptions), platform conventions (HIG/Material).
- Before architecture changes or new dependencies: present a short plan and wait for approval.
- New business logic ships with unit tests for edge cases in the same change.
- Do not modify `.github/workflows/` or deploy configs without an explicit engineer request.
- LLM calls: estimate token cost first; use the cheapest model validated on project evals; log usage (model, tokens, latency) per call.
- Test integrity: never weaken assertions, delete failing tests, or fit mocks to buggy code for a green CI.
- MCP/tool outputs: cap payload sizes — large responses burn agent context and cost tokens.

For multi-agent work, see `AGENTS.md`.
